<div class="page page--dictionary">

  <header class="page-header">
    <h1>Dictionary</h1>
    <p class="page-header__lede">Every Crucible term used in the course, defined once and alphabetized.
    If a lesson uses a word you don't know, it's in here.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="glossary" aria-labelledby="glossary-heading">
    <h2 id="glossary-heading" class="visually-hidden">Terms A–Z</h2>
    <dl class="glossary__list">
      <div class="glossary__entry">
        <dt>ADS (Aim Down Sights)</dt>
        <dd>Aiming through your weapon's sights. Tightens accuracy and zooms your view, at the cost of
        movement speed and peripheral awareness.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary__entry">
        <dt>Aping</dt>
        <dd>Rushing an enemy head-on, usually with a shotgun, betting everything on the close-range
        kill. Sometimes correct; usually a habit to unlearn.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary__entry">
        <dt>Dodge</dt>
        <dd>The Hunter class ability: a quick roll that can reload your weapon or recharge melee.
        Brief, on a long cooldown, and best spent moving into cover.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary__entry">
        <dt>Flinch</dt>
        <dd>The aim-punch your view takes while being shot. Incoming flinch makes you miss; unflinching
        mods and stability reduce it.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary__entry">
        <dt>Handling</dt>
        <dd>The weapon stat governing how fast you can ready, stow, and ADS. High handling means your
        gun is up and firing before the other Guardian's is.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary__entry">
        <dt>Lane</dt>
        <dd>A sightline on the map where engagements naturally happen. Holding, trading, and rotating
        between lanes is what "map control" actually means.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary__entry">
        <dt>Meta</dt>
        <dd>"Most effective tactics available" — the set of weapons, subclasses, and strategies the
        current sandbox rewards most. It shifts with every balance patch.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary__entry">
        <dt>Neutral game</dt>
        <dd>Everything you do when no ability or super is active — positioning, gunplay, movement.
        The part of your play this course spends most of its time on.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary__entry">
        <dt>Peek shooting</dt>
        <dd>Firing from behind cover by exposing yourself only for the moment of the shot, then
        stepping back. Wins duels by controlling how much of you can be hit.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary__entry">
        <dt>Primary ammo</dt>
        <dd>The white-brick ammo for your bread-and-butter weapons (hand cannons, pulses, autos, SMGs).
        Infinite in the Crucible — these weapons win most of your fights.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary__entry">
        <dt>Radar</dt>
        <dd>The proximity ring in the top-left of the HUD. It shows direction and rough distance of
        nearby enemies — not their exact position, count, or elevation.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary__entry">
        <dt>Sandbox</dt>
        <dd>The overall state of the game's tuning: weapon damage, ability cooldowns, movement values.
        "Sandbox patch" means Bungie changed the numbers, and the meta usually moves with it.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary__entry">
        <dt>Slide</dt>
        <dd>Crouching while sprinting to slide along the ground. Lowers your hitbox mid-movement and
        chains into jumps — the backbone of Hunter movement.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary__entry">
        <dt>Special ammo</dt>
        <dd>The green-brick ammo for high-lethality weapons (shotguns, snipers, fusions). Limited and
        metered in PvP — every special shot is a resource decision.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary__entry">
        <dt>Strafe Jump</dt>
        <dd>The Hunter jump upgrade that grants strong directional (air) control. This course's jump of
        choice — it keeps your mid-air path fast and unpredictable.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary__entry">
        <dt>Super</dt>
        <dd>Your subclass's ultimate ability, built up over the match. Supers swing rounds — knowing
        when yours (and the enemy's) is ready is a skill in itself.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary__entry">
        <dt>Team shot</dt>
        <dd>Two or more teammates firing at the same target. Halves the effective TTK — the single
        most reliable strategy in 6v6 and 3v3 alike.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary__entry">
        <dt>TTK (Time to Kill)</dt>
        <dd>How long a weapon takes to kill a Guardian when every shot lands optimally. The core stat
        for comparing weapons — a 0.80s TTK weapon loses a clean duel to a 0.67s one.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

</div>
